// Title: HackTool - SharpEvtMute Execution
// Sigma ID: bedfc8ad-d1c7-4e37-a20e-e2b0dbee759c
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-09-07 | Modified: 2023-02-14
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685.001
// Description: Detects the use of SharpEvtHook, a tool that tampers with the Windows event logs
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/bats3c/EvtMute
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hktl_sharpevtmute.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\SharpEvtMute.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoFileDescription =~ "SharpEvtMute" or (ProcessCommandLine contains "--Filter \"rule " or ProcessCommandLine contains "--Encoded --Filter \\\"")
